### Chapter 3: Working with Data 

Standard data organization (an most importantly scrubbing is completed in excel. 
Excel and R communicate in the wave forms of .csv files, or Comma Separated Values. R uses the function "read.csv" to load in these files. Using 
Dr. Stitch's "ctr_fish.csv" let's load one in. 

# Start by reading in the data
am_shad <- read.csv("data/ctr_fish.csv")

Sweet no issues (because working directory was set correctly). Now this data file is pretty substantial so instead of burning our eyes with thousands
of rows, let's take a simplistic look using the head function. 

# Look at the first 10 rows
head(am_shad, 10)

Our console should now display our data like so: 

